# Moved from bootstrap/examples/assumed-need-coherent.moss. Verdicts below credited to the
# oracle are the old Rocq oracle's (moss_m2, removed when moss-ref replaced
# it), so they are historical; the suite checks the current verdicts.
# AssumesComplete (AUDIT-CHANGES #57; D20; criteria section 6, fidelity).
# Each assumed item's requirements are in force and its own needs provided.
# Here: f needs h at T = U (through context H); g assumes H and f, so h is in force at that instantiation.
# Audit before: accepts. Audit now: accepts (argued from the rules, not run).
# Oracle (moss_m2): accepts.
# Native (ob-family moss, seed 1h1710x0): accepts.
type T;
type U;
assume T { fn h(); }
context H = U, h[T = U];
assume H { fn f(); }
assume H, f { fn g() {} }
fn main() {}
